{{Quote|With enough credits you can do anything.|[[Treze]], to [[Yana Ro]]|<ref name="Path of Deceit">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref>}}
The '''Galactic Credit Standard''',<ref name="Dok">{{GEAttr|Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities}}</ref> also known as the '''galactic credit''' or simply the '''credit''', was a standardized form of [[currency]] in use throughout the [[Galactic Republic]],<ref name="TPM" /> the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="ANH">{{Film|IV}}</ref> and territories of the [[New Republic]], [[Resistance]], and other non-aligned [[Star system|systems]] following the [[Imperial Instruments of Surrender|fall of the Empire]].<ref name="Last Jedi Junior">''[[Star Wars: The Last Jedi: A Junior Novel]]''</ref> Credits were considered acceptable as currency on most major [[planet]]s, though on some planets in the [[Outer Rim Territories]], such as [[Tatooine]], some merchants refused to accept them, desiring something "more real" in exchange for their goods. They were sometimes referred to as "'''Republic credits'''" or "'''Republic dataries'''" during the [[time]] [[Republic Era|of the Galactic Republic]].<ref name="TPM">{{Film|I}}</ref> "'''Creds'''" was a colloquial term for credits,<ref name="idiots">{{Rebels|Idiot's Array (episode)}}</ref> as was "'''decs'''."<ref name="Barrier subs">{{SkeletonCrew|Way, Way Out Past the Barrier}} {{Subtitles|Disney+}}</ref> The credit symbol ([[File:AurebeshSans-Serif_credit.png]]) resembled an [[Aurebesh]] letter R with two vertical strokes at the top.<ref name="swc">''[[Star Wars: Commander]]''</ref>

During the [[Clone Wars]], the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]] issued its own '''Confederacy credits'''.<ref name="newdawn">[[A New Dawn (novel)|''A New Dawn'']]</ref> The old Republic currency was discontinued and exchanged with '''Imperial credits''' during the [[Imperial Era|Age of the Empire]].<ref name="AbEverything">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> Following the [[Battle of Endor]], credits were known as '''New Republic credits''' as the [[New Republic]] replaced the Empire as the galactic government.<ref name="Alphabet Squadron">[[Alphabet Squadron (novel)|''Alphabet Squadron'']]</ref> The citizens of [[Milvayne]] used '''Milvayne credits'''.<ref name="Aphra 26">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 26|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 26]]</ref>

[[Credit ingot]]s were a physical form of credits.<ref name="Darth Vader 8">[[Darth Vader (2015) 8|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 8]]</ref> Credit ingots were small, flat, rectangular bars of [[Color|gold]]- and silver-colored metal, the silver ones a bit longer than the gold ones. Symbols were stamped onto their surface, including the credit symbol ({{Cr}}).<ref name="Corruption">{{TCW|Corruption (episode)}}</ref> Another means of carrying credits was through [[credit chip]]s.<ref name="whatwookiee">[[Star Wars: What is a Wookiee? (2015)|''What is a Wookiee?'']]</ref>

The [[decicred]], or "dime," was a unit of currency worth one tenth of a full Republic credit.<ref name="EpGuide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode006.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: Downfall of a Droid}}</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Republic credits? Republic credits are no good out here; I need something more real.|Watto to Qui-Gon Jinn|<ref name="TPM" />}}
[[File:MandoCurrency-Corruption.png|thumb|right|250px|A bribe of Republic credit ingots, given to a [[Unidentified Mandalorian customs official|Mandalorian customs official]]<ref name="Corruption" />]]
Credits could be carried on a person via [[credit chip]]s.<ref name="gamble">''[[Ezra's Gamble]]''</ref> Credits also came in the form of [[credit ingot]]s, which were often kept in vaults and [[transport]]ed under heavy guard. During the [[Imperial Era|Age of the Empire]], [[Arquitens-class light cruiser|''Arquitens''-class light cruisers]] were often used for this task.<ref name="Darth Vader 8">[[Darth Vader (2015) 8|''Darth Vader'' (2015) 8]]</ref>

One [[merchant]] who was wary of the value of credits was [[Watto]], who refused [[Qui-Gon Jinn]]'s offer of 20,000 credits in exchange for a [[T-14 hyperdrive generator]].<ref name="TPM" />

[[File:CreditIngot-TheVoxxVortex5000.png|thumb|left|300px|A stack of credits paid to [[Team Colossus]], by [[Vranki]]<ref name="The Voxx Vortex 5000">{{Resistance|The Voxx Vortex 5000}}</ref>]]
The [[mercenary]] [[AD-W4]] considered credits to be the highest power and true ruler of [[the galaxy]], even more powerful than a [[Deity|god]].<ref name="Mace Windu 1">[[Jedi of the Republic – Mace Windu 1|''Jedi of the Republic – Mace Windu'' 1]]</ref> Similarly, the [[Evereni]] [[Yana Ro]] believed credits were the only power that every being in the galaxy could respect.<ref name="Path of Deceit">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref> While credits were highly coveted by many, this sentiment was not shared by all. Jedi Knight [[Tensu Run]] was one example, stating that there were things even credits couldn't buy, like thoughts.<ref name="Inquisitors 4">[[Inquisitors 4|''Inquisitors'' 4]]</ref> The Sith Lord [[Maul|Darth Maul]] was another example, as he made clear when hiring pirates from the [[Ohnaka Gang]] in the [[Florrum system]].<ref name="Revival">{{TCW|Revival (episode)}}</ref>

After the [[Proclamation of the New Order|formation]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Galactic Republic]] credits were phased out within [[Standard day|days]], with Imperial citizens induced to register for identifying [[chain code]]s in order to exchange their now-worthless [[currency]] for Imperial credits.<ref name="Cut and Run">{{TBB|Cut and Run}}</ref> Eventually, credits from the [[time]] of the Republic became mostly worthless.<ref name="crimson">{{StoryCite|story=The Crimson Corsair and the Lost Treasure of Count Dooku|book=Tales from a Galaxy Far, Far Away: Aliens: Volume I}}</ref> Credits from the Galactic Empire likewise became worthless following the rise of the [[New Republic]], to the point that [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]] was forced to pay the [[bounty hunter]] [[Mercurial Swift]] "in owed favors."<ref name="lifedebt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref> The New Republic also issued credits, but their value became volatile in [[34 ABY]] following the [[Hosnian Cataclysm]]. Consequently, the city of [[Canto Bight]] prohibited New Republic credits and required all visitors to exchange their credits for currency made of [[aurodium]].<ref name="Complete Visual New">''[[Star Wars: The Complete Visual Dictionary, New Edition]]''</ref>

Hoping to win the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'', the [[smuggler]] [[Han Solo]] once tracked [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] to a [[jungle outpost]] on [[Numidian Prime]] and played him in a game of [[sabacc]]. A bronze credit was used in the [[sabacc pot]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

When attempting to secure passage to [[Alderaan]] aboard the ''Millennium Falcon'', [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] stressed to Han Solo the importance of avoiding "Imperial entanglements." Concerned with the danger, Solo asked for 10,000 credits up front. As Kenobi and [[Luke Skywalker]] did not have much with them, Kenobi instead negotiated an upfront price of 2,000 credits with the promise of an additional 15,000 upon safe arrival at Alderaan. Solo deemed it worth the risk, as he and his partner [[Chewbacca]] were heavily in debt to [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] the [[Hutt]] and had a [[bounty]] on them.<ref name="ANH" />

[[File:New_Republic_Credits_TBOBF1.png|thumb|right|300px|Garsa Fwip filled Boba Fett's helmet with New Republic credits.]]
Credits were also used to give tribute to a person of importance. When former bounty hunter [[Boba Fett]] became a new [[crime lord]], dignitaries such as [[Garfalaquox]] and [[Garsa Fwip]] offered tribute in the form of New Republic credits to him.<ref name="Chapter 1: Stranger in a Strange Land" />

Around 34 ABY, the shop [[Dok-Ondar's Den of Antiquities]] at [[Black Spire Outpost]] on [[Batuu]] sold individual, mint-condition Imperial credits to collectors.<ref name="Dok" />

==Behind the scenes==
Credits first appeared in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']]<ref name="ANH" /> before being identified in the [[1999]] film [[Star Wars: Episode I The Phantom Menace|''Star Wars'': Episode I ''The Phantom Menace'']].<ref name="TPM" /> Credits is the form of currency in the [[1971]] film [[Wikipedia:THX 1138|''THX 1138'']], which was written by the creator of ''[[Star Wars]]'', [[George Lucas]], and his friend [[Walter Murch]] at [[Wikipedia:American Zoetrope|American Zoetrope]].<ref name="THX 1138">[[Wikipedia:THX 1138|''THX 1138'']]. Dir. [[George Lucas]]. [[Warner Bros.]] [[1971]]. Film.</ref>

